  "description": "Water at the response_h2o_raman_tpa geometry, HF, one rung (protocol 1e-4, k 6): two RPA excited states (omega 0.3223886, 0.3832919) and their 2PA D_linear (2.49802, 21.00695), from the cold guess. The unseeded half of the pair with response_h2o_tpa_seeded; together they measure what a DALTON seed buys. requested_properties [] drops the static alpha legs the default would add (2PA needs only the legs at omega_f/2). Response dconv 1e-4, not the Raman case's 1e-3: at 1e-3 (5e-3 gates) the seeded run stopped after 3 ES iterations 2.8e-4 from the cold omega and 1.7% off in D, so the pair measured where each run stopped rather than how fast it converged. The reference (1f84425ca) predates the relative FD gate (2a3d92920, gate 5*dconv*(1 + ||x||)): there every FD leg exited at bsh 3.5-4.9e-4 (absolute gate 5e-4), ES 11 iterations, 6 FD legs 108 iterations, 25 envelope iterations. Under the relative gate the legs stop near 1e-3 (drop 5: bsh 0.92-1.11e-3, 73 leg iterations), and since D-122 (KAIN from the start of a cold excited-state main solve) the ES solve takes 10. Caps: envelope 30, ES 14. Reference: RelWithDebInfo, Pthreads, ArmPL, 1 rank x 7 threads, dd (Neoverse-N1), 2026-09-24, at 1f84425ca, wall 3319 s (concurrent with the seeded case and a CI runner). omega tol 1e-3 au, D_linear rtol 2e-2. Nightly tier.",
